<title>USA: YEN REFLECTS JAPAN'S FUNDAMENTALS, IMF SAYS.</title>
<headline>YEN REFLECTS JAPAN'S FUNDAMENTALS, IMF SAYS.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The current level of the yen is well supported by Japan's economic fundamentals, and the country should keep interest rates down until later in the year, the International Monetary Fund (IMF) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Directors believed that the current level of the yen was broadly in line with fundamentals,&quot; the IMF's Executive Board said in its annual review of the Japanese economy.</p>
</text>
